From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375-motorola-rhodep: add the charger

Add the SGM41542 at 0x3b so the battery actually charges. Until now the
gauge reported correctly but the charger sat with charging disabled in
REG01 and its watchdog off, so the state persisted across reboots and the
phone ran off VBUS without ever charging the cell.

The charge limits are deliberately below what the vendor allows. Downstream
goes up to 4450 mV / 3000 mA, but only because it runs a software JEITA
loop (enable_sw_jeita in its sgm4154x node) that lowers the target and cuts
the current with temperature, and stops charging outside 0..50 C. There is
no equivalent loop here, so the temperate-zone values from that same table
Full charge uses the vendor's jeita_temp_t2_to_t3 voltage (4450 mV, rounded
down to 4448 mV by the 32 mV step). The hot side of JEITA is enforced by the
kernel through the battery-thermal zone and the cold side by a userspace
service, so the full voltage is safe. 

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -152,6 +152,19 @@
 		charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <5000000>;
 		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3400000>;
 		voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4450000>;
+
+		/*
+		 * Full charge voltage from the vendor JEITA table
+		 * (jeita_temp_t2_to_t3). The chip's 32 mV step rounds 4450 down
+		 * to 4448 mV. The hot side of JEITA is enforced by the kernel
+		 * through the battery-thermal zone below (charge current is
+		 * throttled at 45 C and stopped at 50 C), and the cold side by
+		 * the rhodep-battery-jeita service, so the full voltage is safe.
+		 */
+		constant-charge-voltage-max-microvolt = <4450000>;
+		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <1250000>;
+		precharge-current-microamp = <300000>;
+		charge-term-current-microamp = <240000>;
 	};
 
 	touch_avdd: touch-avdd-regulator {
@@ -201,6 +214,27 @@
 		shunt-resistor-micro-ohms = <5000>;
 		cellwise,ui-full-soc = <97>;
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * SGM41542: register level clone of the bq25601. Checked against the
+	 * vendor header (same masks, steps and bases for IINDPM, VINDPM,
+	 * VBATREG, ITERM and ICHG) and against the hardware: an unconfigured
+	 * fabrica leia 0x58 = 4208 mV, identico a BQ2560X_VBATREG_DEF_uV.
+	 *
+	 * Without "ti,watchdog-timeout-ms" the driver leaves the watchdog off,
+	 * which is what we want: if it expires the part resets its registers to
+	 * the factory values and charging stops.
+	 *
+	 * The interrupt (tlmm 12 in the vendor DT) is left out on purpose: it is
+	 * optional in bq256xx and without it the driver reads the registers on
+	 * demand. It can be added later.
+	 */
+	charger@3b {
+		compatible = "sgm,sgm41542";
+		reg = <0x3b>;
+		monitored-battery = <&battery>;
+		input-current-limit-microamp = <1000000>;
+	};
 };
 
 &i2c10 {
